# Python
#
# Interpreter droppings only. The setuptools packaging rules that used to sit
# here (var/, eggs/, sdist/, wheels/, parts/, /lib/, *.egg-info, ...) came from
# the stock Python template and outlived the packaged backend that needed them.
# They were not harmless: "var/" carries no slash, so git matched it at every
# depth and silently dropped workflow-lib/plugins/{cpp,go,python,rust,ts}/var -
# the var.* workflow plugin - from every commit. Nothing here builds a Python
# distribution any more, so the rules are gone rather than anchored.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Build output (JavaScript; emitted at many depths, so deliberately unanchored)
build/
dist/

# Virtual environment
venv/
ENV/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

